I’ll create a function to generate signed upload headers that include the signature and expiry. In the initialization response, I’ll set the headers to include the content type along with the signature headers.

The URL will then be `${origin}/documents/${documentId}/upload`. The PUT route needs to read the headers and validate the signature by computing an HMAC from the storage key. This approach avoids exposing the signature in the URL and helps prevent logging issues. We also need to ensure server logs do not print headers. Finally, we should remove the existing `/uploads` endpoint and adjust the current code to no longer return a signed URL with a signature query.
